   "source": [
    "# 3.12/3.17 Pointing -- Update VIS Pointing Loop"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bf48f4ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "OVERVIEW: Update the VIS pointing parameters in the control loop. Observe three stars in the same FOV with moderate brightness to quantify the pointing performance with new parameters in arcsecs/time. A long duration observation enables measurement during possible thermal variations over ~1 orbit: 100 min / 6000 sec. \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "CHECK: The data should measure the pointing accuracy (absolute) and precision (rms variation from nominal) in arcseconds over time. \n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "EXIT CRITERIA: observation obtained, analysis complete and summarized in 3.12/3.17_ResultsSummary.md\n",
    "- pointing accuracy required = ?\n",
    "- precision required = ?\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA: three 200x200 regions of interest (ROIs) on VISDA, one long-duration observation\n",
    "- Note - data volume may be reduced by reducing temporal resolution\n",
    "    \n",
    "    \n",
    "TARGET CRITERIA: 3 stars in the same VIDSA FOV, One in the center and two others at least 1/3 from the center in different directions from the center. Moderately bright targets with Pandora Mag 8-9 (approx Gaia B Mag). This magnitude criteria is flexible and currently being refined -- our science target list is selected for Jmag=7-11.5 and Hmag<11.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "KEY STAKEHOLDERS: Tom Barclay"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "3c7de336",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "OUTSTANDING QUESTIONS\n",
    "- target selection\n",
    "- numerical pointing and precision accuracy requirement"
   ]
  },
